AUTH-007 | Authentication & Security | Single Sign-On | Functional | MISSING | No SSO implementation was found during project inspection. | Implement SSO integration architecture for an enterprise identity provider, subject to deployment requirements.

AUTH-008 | Authentication & Security | Session management | Functional | COMPLETE | JWT token_version security, refresh-token validation, token blacklist support, and session invalidation are implemented. | Continue testing and migrate dependent views to the DB-driven authorization model.

AUTH-009 | Authentication & Security | Device/session management | Functional | PARTIAL | User session listing, individual session revocation, all-session revocation, OutstandingToken and BlacklistedToken tracking are implemented. | Device-specific metadata such as user agent/device identity and session location is not yet established.

AUTH-010 | Authentication & Security | Account lockout | Functional | COMPLETE | Secure login tracks failed attempts and temporarily locks accounts after 5 consecutive failures for 15 minutes. | Add/expand automated security tests if coverage is incomplete.

AUTH-011 | Authentication & Security | Password policies | Functional | COMPLETE | Django password validators are configured and PasswordChangeView explicitly invokes validate_password(). | Verify policy presentation/administration requirements later if configurable password policies are required.

AUTH-012 | Authentication & Security | Security alerts | Functional | PARTIAL | Login success, login failure, account lockout, password change, session revocation, and refresh-token reuse events are written to AuditLog. | No user-facing security-alert/notification mechanism has been established.

AUTH-013 | Authentication & Security | Role management | Functional | PARTIAL | DB-driven Role, Permission, RolePermission, and UserRole models plus authorization services and permission classes exist. | Role administration and migration away from legacy user.role checks are incomplete.

AUTH-014 | Authentication & Security | Role + Permission system; roles must not be hard-coded | Architecture | PARTIAL | Database-driven authorization infrastructure and HasPermission exist, with seeded enterprise roles and permissions. | Many modules still use legacy user.role checks and current users have no UserRole assignments; complete migration and assignment strategy is required.


